// Zero-sum properties of the soldier/sniper "skirmish" (hide-or-run) game (see also ../qualitative/skirmish.prism).
// Reaching "home" (s=2) has value 1 for the soldier only in the limit: no optimal strategy exists, only
// near-optimal ones (run with a small probability). Value iteration converges slowly (about 1/k), so the
// expected results are PRISM's values at the default -epsilon, not the limit 1.

// RESULT: 0.999000999005989
<<p1>>Pmax=? [ F s=2 ]

// the sniper now plays the runner's role (the value is again 1 in the limit)
// RESULT: 0.999000999005989
<<p1>>Pmin=? [ F s=2 ]

// the sniper cannot force "wet": the soldier just never runs
// RESULT: 0.0
<<p2>>Pmax=? [ F s=1 ]

// RESULT: 1.0
<<p1>>Pmax=? [ G !(s=1) ]
